## Worked violation → fix

**Violation** (CLI):

```rust
fn cmd_set(config: &AppConfig, key: &str, value: &str) {
    let _ = config.backend.put(key, value, false);
    println!("ok");
}
```

**Fix**:

```rust
fn cmd_set(config: &AppConfig, key: &str, value: &str) -> std::process::ExitCode {
    match config.set_value(key, value) {
        Ok(()) => {
            println!("ok");
            std::process::ExitCode::SUCCESS
        }
        Err(AppConfigError::UnknownKey { key, manifest }) => {
            eprintln!(
                "error: unknown configuration key '{key}' for program '{manifest}'\n\
                 The active manifest does not declare this key. See `… list` for the full key set."
            );
            std::process::ExitCode::from(2)
        }
        Err(AppConfigError::InvalidValue { key, reason, manifest }) => {
            eprintln!("error: invalid value for '{key}' in '{manifest}': {reason}");
            std::process::ExitCode::from(3)
        }
        Err(AppConfigError::Storage(e)) => {
            eprintln!("error: storage backend failure writing '{key}': {e:#}");
            std::process::ExitCode::from(4)
        }
    }
}
```

The CLI now refuses typos with a clear message AND a documented
exit code. The configurator GUI calls the same `set_value` and
surfaces the same error variants in its status pane.

